<p>The United States was awaiting Iran’s response to a proposed short-term deal to halt the two-month war, reopen the Strait of Hormuz and create a 30-day window for negotiations on a broader settlement, according to Iranian officials cited by The New York Times and Pakistani officials involved in mediation. The framework centers on a one-page memorandum rather than a full peace agreement, leaving disputes over Iran’s nuclear program, uranium stockpiles, sanctions relief and the length of any halt to nuclear work unresolved. President Trump said talks had been positive and warned that bombing would resume if Tehran rejected the terms, while Iran’s foreign ministry said the proposal remained under review and one Iranian spokesperson described it as “more of an American wish-list than a reality”. The diplomacy followed a near breakdown of the current ceasefire and continued tension around the Strait of Hormuz, including reports of U.S. military action against an Iranian-flagged tanker and exchanges of fire in the waterway.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/KAj1oClCcFTOEq1x0mtofb_DcAfQ83Mk6nDS8cJbnLE4i5xrNi7Cu5gMI2m71frZR0ihoS3eED3fksRPmbaOPYVjRQPWt1g5VwHJ1uzLN6jeVAheJxpEgLI1WJmRHx_4GKVNRYS0nUS3YgiZL1jr9xK3PGAcbUOesv5s5V7mhAX9CjvzAwDorzJ4PoQ5So-haIRbM4mGSGfbrkQXXb6F6Wa-1ykGIIL6AwXnlAjA9gUotl91Ip6uX_9_3iYUv4kF_K7gRIFDNmHg_UMxBA2dHsbHfhFM' alt='Cargo ships sit at anchor in the Strait of Hormuz.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Internal review: News18 reported that Iran’s power structure discussed the amended framework, including in consultations with advisers close to Mojtaba Khamenei.</li><li>Market moves: Asian and global stocks rose while oil prices fell or steadied as traders assessed whether shipping disruptions through Hormuz could ease.</li><li>Regional spillover: An extension of the U.S.-Iran ceasefire could affect Lebanon, where a truce with Israel faced new pressure after a strike on southern Beirut killed a Hezbollah commander.</li></ul><blockquote>Ou